From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:29:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 11/19] Add GPU-owner tests for the 32-row GEMV and bs1 greedy
 equality

test_gemv32.py (adapted from wt-tree's test_gemv16.py) checks rows 1-32 against
reconstruct + hgemm with fp16 and fp32 output at U = 1/2/4. It checks the
upper row tiles separately, checks that a row's value is bit-identical at
every row tile (8/16/32), times WMMA against the cooperative fallback, and
checks the fused gate+up mgemm at 9-32 rows. It also checks that the graphed
BC GatedMLP's replays at 1-32 rows equal its eager first call.

test_greedy_equal.py writes the greedy DFlash2 token ids of one checkout
(TabbyAPI-like setup: Q4 caches, max_history = draft tokens), and --compare
checks two runs token for token. Prompts stay above 32 tokens, since a
9-32-token prefill now runs the WMMA GEMV and rounds differently by design.

Both load the model and run kernels; the GPU owner runs them.

